<!--
  Geometry  : water cylinder R = 16962.280 mm, H = 36378.422 mm (z from -H/2 to +H/2, axis = z)
              11096 SK ID PMTs (barrel 7752, top 1672, bottom 1672), positions snapped to the wall
              exactly as LUCiD Cylinder.from_pmt_file(snap_to_wall=True).
              sensor = sphere r = 254.0 mm centred ON the wall, clipped by the wall (dome into the water);
              caps clipped by a plane 0.1 mm inside the wall, barrel by two chords
              (half-angle 0.428989 deg) 0.1 mm inside the wall -> no overlap with volWater.
              copynumber = LUCiD sensor index (barrel, top, bottom order = row of detector.all_points).
              SK cable/pmt_id for each copynumber is in SK_LUCiD_opticks_pmtmap.csv.
  Optics    : water n = 1.33, ABSLENGTH / RAYLEIGH / MIEHG(g = 0.95) from materials/water.json
              as LUCiD wavelength mode evaluates them; EFFICIENCY = pmt/SK_QE.json (qe_corrections = 1.0).
  Surfaces  : Opticks-representable subset of SK_physics_config.json (pair with sensor_reflection_rate = 0,
              wall_fspec = 0 in LUCiD):  wall dielectric_metal REFLECTIVITY 0.05, 100% Lambertian;
              PMT dielectric_metal REFLECTIVITY 0, EFFICIENCY = QE(lambda).
  Sensors   : SensDet = PhotonDetector on volPMTbarrel / volPMTcap. No '_' in the LV names and unnamed
              physvols (-> "<LV>_PV"), so OpticalSims' MySensorIdentifier gives Opticks the copy number
              as sensor id.  Opticks hit sensor_id = LUCiD index.
-->
